eally dig deep do the  excavation to figure out what motivates  you what do you care about more than  money those are your values and those  should be driving what you're how you're  spending your time since you referenced  us i feel like we got a case study over  here in nate burleson and how to make  career changes boldly former nfl player  uh then you did some local hits in  detroit on television then you were  working for x extra yeah now you're  working for us you know all about this  you could give the master class on no no  well i love you what do you say when you  talk about picking lanes and that's  perfect segue tony because  when i was younger i think we all  experienced it what do you want to be  when you grow up that's usually singular  you get to high school you know what do  you want to study in college and you're  done with college what job do you want  to all these things right and you say  pick your lanes and in the illustration  there's 14 fill in the blanks yes which  means you can do multiple things you can  wear multiple hats because you you don't  know how something fits until you try it  on that's right and why do you think  that's important for everybody to know  you don't have to pick one lane  by the way i left out jobs in that  little summary of what you do  all aboard  he's a graphic designer yeah yeah  there's a lot of double devils  just the shoulders off a little bit so  you're you are the consummate  multi-hyphenate and i think you  represent sort of a new definition of  success for a new generation of of  people entering the job market they want  to  figure out what they're good at which  sometimes takes some exploration and  then they want to have the freedom and  flexibility to try new things and to  build a career that is fulfilling first  and foremost um and to fail if you if  because i feel like people don't want to  fail that's right you're going to stub  your toe occasionally and that's okay  and and you're going to get your 